  "description": "Interop between NumSharp NDArray and TorchSharp tensors (.NET bindings for libtorch, the engine under PyTorch). nd.AsTensor() hands a NumSharp buffer to libtorch without copying - any non-negative-stride layout, broadcast views as torch's own expand - and tensor.AsNDArray() views a CPU tensor's storage as an NDArray. Each verb takes a TorchCodecMode: Auto (view when possible, else a copy), View (sharing or an exception) or Copy (always independent). Dtypes without a counterpart cross by NumPy's NEP 50 promotion; libtorch's deleter releases the NumSharp buffer when the last tensor over it is freed. Conversion library only: no engine backend, no ModuleInitializer, no native asset of its own (it binds TorchSharp's LibTorchSharp).",
